  "body": "_⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟠 Major_ | _⚡ Quick win_\n\n**마스터카드 prefix 검증이 길이 조건 때문에 우회됩니다.**\n\n두 번째 자리 검증이 `value.length === 2`일 때만 수행되어, 예를 들어 `56xx`를 한 번에 입력하면 오류 없이 통과할 수 있습니다. 두 자리 이상 입력된 경우에도 동일 prefix 규칙이 적용되는지 점검해 주세요.\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nIn `@app/src/validators/CardValidator.ts` around lines 15 - 18, The Mastercard\nprefix check in CardValidator currently only runs when value.length === 2,\nletting inputs like \"56xx\" bypass validation; update the condition to check for\nat least two characters (use value.length >= 2) or otherwise ensure the\nsecond-digit check runs whenever value[1] is defined, keeping the existing tests\non value[0] === \"5\" and ![\"1\",\"2\",\"3\",\"4\",\"5\"].includes(value[1]) so the prefix\nrule applies for any input length; modify the logic inside the CardValidator\nmethod that uses the value variable (the block with value.length === 2 &&\nvalue[0] === \"5\" && ![\"1\",\"2\",\"3\",\"4\",\"5\"].includes(value[1])) accordingly.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- fingerprinting:phantom:poseidon:hawk:a6a7d778-f54a-4c07-b8c4-fb36327d06fe -->\n\n<!-- 4e71b3a2 -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit -->",
